  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd17 Direct Login Link\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Click here to sign in to My Service Canada Account (MSCA)](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd10 Sign-In Options\n\nYou can log in using **one of the following methods**:\n\n1. **GCKey**\n   GCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner (Banking credentials)**\n   Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In (Alberta & BC only)**\n   You can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. This service is only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb New User? How to Register\n\nIf you don't have an account yet, you'll need:\n- A Social Insurance Number (SIN) to create an account.\n- A Personal Access Code (PAC) \u2014 a 7-digit code used to verify your identity, which you need to request from Service Canada.\n- By clicking \"Start your registration,\" you will be able to create a GCKey username and password if you don't already have one.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Reminder\nAccess and use MSCA only as yourself \u2014 no one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\nIf you need further help, visit the official page: [canada.ca/my-account](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)",
